q: write a java code to return rebuilded message that has been split in string of an array. rules are : first part will always start with 'A' and last character of rebuild message will be 'Z'
two strigs can only be merged when last character of first string and first character of last string is same and will print only once.

ex: Ab, bZ : output : AbZ
ex: ...../, A----., /---Z : op: A----..../---Z

------------------------------------------------------------------
Logic:Store every string in a HashMap
| Key | Value    |
| --- | -------- |
| '.' | "...../" |
| 'A' | "A----." |
| '/' | "/---Z"  |
Think it like dictionary
2.Find the starting string
3.Look at the last character
4.Find the next string and Merge Them
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        String[] arr1 = {"bZ", "Ab"};
        System.out.println(rebuildMessage(arr1));

        String[] arr2 = {"...../", "A----.", "/---Z"};
        System.out.println(rebuildMessage(arr2));
    }

    public static String rebuildMessage(String[] arr) {

        Map<Character, String> map = new HashMap<>();

        String current = null;

        // Store strings in map and find the starting string
        for (String s : arr) {
            map.put(s.charAt(0), s);

            if (s.charAt(0) == 'A') {
                current = s;
            }
        }

        if (current == null) {
            return "Invalid Input";
        }

        while (current.charAt(current.length() - 1) != 'Z') {

            char last = current.charAt(current.length() - 1);

            String next = map.get(last);

            if (next == null) {
                return "Cannot rebuild";
            }

            // Merge without duplicating the common character
            current = current + next.substring(1);
        }

        return current;
    }
}
